{"schema":1,"function":"gamma_cdf","description":"Gamma distribution cumulative distribution function P(a, x) (shape a, rate 1); chi-squared with df = 2a at 2x","inputs":["a","x"],"outputs":["y"],"points":538,"tolerance":{"rel":1e-12,"reason":"With rate 1 this is P(a, x), the function of the gammainc dataset, so it gets gammainc's tolerance (accepted by the owner, to be revisited). The condition number |x f(x) / P| reaches 3.0e4 (a = 1e6, x = a - 30 sqrt(a)), so a method that rounds x / a loses up to 3.3e-12 there; one that forms x - a exactly (Sterbenz's lemma, a/2 <= x <= 2a) and expands in (x - a) / a, as Temme's uniform expansion does (DLMF 8.12; Boost), loses only about k^2 2^-53 at x = a + k sqrt(a) (1e-13 at k = 30), so 1e-12 demands such a method. SciPy's worst error here is 3.5e-13 (a = 1000, x = 500), except 2.1e-10 at a = 1e6, x = 990000 (P = 5.4e-24; the finite sum DLMF 8.4.10 confirms mpmath) and a subnormal result flushed to 0 at a = 50, x = 1e-5. Results below 2.2e-308 are judged relative to that number (conventions)"},"grid":"a in {0.01, 0.1, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2, 3, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 1e3, 1e4, 1e5, 1e6} x x in {0, 1e-300, 1e-100, 1e-20, 1e-10, 1e-5, 1e-3, 0.01, 0.1, 0.5, 1, 2, 5, 10, 20, 50, 100, 200, 500, 700, 750, 1e3, 1e4, 1e5, 1e6, 1e7, 1e10, 1e300}, plus x = a + k sqrt(a) (rounded to a double) for k in {-30, -10, -3, -1, 1, 3, 10, 30} where positive","mpmath":{"version":"1.4.1","dps":[50,100]},"scipy":{"version":"1.18.1","function":"scipy.stats.gamma.cdf"},"numpy":"2.5.4","python":"3.13"}
